    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d232">

                <pb facs="0437" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg179"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1880</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sharp</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1545]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Paris</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-10-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">October 29, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received November 10.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In confirmation of my telegram No. 1064 of
                    the 26th inst.,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d232-f1"/> I have the honor to transmit
                    herewith in copy and translation a report <pb facs="0438" n="180" xml:id="pg180"
                    /> presented by the President of the Council, Minister for Foreign Affairs, and
                    the Minister of Marine to the President of the Republic on the subject of
                    difficulties in the application of Article 57 of the Declaration of London, as
                    well as the decree which was based upon this report.</p>
                <p>From this it appears that the French Government no longer intends to follow the
                    provisions of Article 57 of the Declaration of London.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wm. G. Sharp</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d232-a1.xml" xpointer="d232-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d232-a2.xml" xpointer="d232-a2"/>
            </div>
